# Eigen deployment configuration.
# For a Docker install. Developing with Bun needs no env file: the API reads .env.development, and .env overrides it.
# The easy way:  ./eigen setup asks the setup questions and writes .env.production.
#                Rerunning it keeps your answers and every key it does not know.
# Manual:        edit .env.production (keep the EIGEN_* lines bootstrap wrote), then run ./eigen setup again.

# === REQUIRED ===
# Your web address, like eigen.example.com.
DOMAIN=
# Address suffix for mailboxes (alice@MAIL_DOMAIN). Empty = DOMAIN. Set it to your apex (like example.com)
# when the web address is a subdomain but mail uses the apex. Every account's address is made on it, so it cannot
# change after the first setup: the API refuses to start on another one.
MAIL_DOMAIN=
# Contact address for Let's Encrypt. Left empty, Caddy uses admin@MAIL_DOMAIN, or admin@DOMAIN without one.
ACME_EMAIL=

# === DEPLOYMENT SHAPE ===
# Pick which optional services run:
#   edge,mail   = bundled Caddy + bundled mail (default, all-in-one)
#   static,mail = bundled frontend container + bundled mail (use with your own webserver)
#   edge        = bundled Caddy only, no mail hosted here (set MAIL_ENABLED=0)
#   static      = bundled frontend only, no mail hosted here (set MAIL_ENABLED=0)
COMPOSE_PROFILES=edge,mail
# 1 when Eigen hosts mail (the 'mail' profile), 0 when it does not: the apps then drop the Mail app,
# its palette entries, the "Mail to..." actions and the IMAP settings card.
MAIL_ENABLED=1
# Where the bundled static container is bound on the host. Your host webserver proxies
# to ${EIGEN_STATIC_HOST}:${EIGEN_STATIC_PORT}. Only used with the 'static' profile.
#   127.0.0.1 = localhost-only (recommended when proxy is on the same host)
#   0.0.0.0   = exposed on all interfaces (LAN-reachable)
EIGEN_STATIC_HOST=127.0.0.1
EIGEN_STATIC_PORT=8080

# === OUTGOING MAIL RELAY (optional) ===
# With hosted mail, Postfix sends through this relay; useful when your provider blocks outbound port 25.
# Without hosted mail, Eigen sends through it itself. Without one, it sends no email: no two-factor codes by
# email, guest sign-in codes, share and access-request notifications, "Email collaborators", waitlist
# invitations, calendar invitations or RSVP replies.
# Port 465 is implicit TLS, any other port STARTTLS. Set the user and password both or neither; with them,
# mail only goes over TLS, and without hosted mail Eigen also checks the relay's certificate.
# With hosted mail, the relay must accept every address on MAIL_DOMAIN, since Postfix sends each user's mail
# from their own address.
# SMTP_RELAY_HOST=smtp-relay.brevo.com
# SMTP_RELAY_PORT=587
# SMTP_RELAY_USER=
# SMTP_RELAY_PASSWORD=

# === DERIVED (setup writes these from DOMAIN; docker-compose.yml sets PRODUCTION=1) ===
# API_URL=https://eigen.example.com
# VITE_API_HOST=/eigen, VITE_APP_ADMIN_URL=/admin and the other app paths stay relative, so the apps work on any
# host name (public domain, LAN IP, tunnel). TRUSTED_NETWORKS comes from EIGEN_SUBNET in docker-compose.yml.

# === ADVANCED ===
# Setup does not ask for these. Add a key to .env.production, then run ./eigen setup again.
# Extra Compose settings go in docker-compose.override.yml; docker/SETUP-GUIDE.md has examples.
#
# The Docker network of the services and the mail resolver's address in it. Setup always writes both, on a /24 no other
# Docker network uses; change them in .env.production if a network added later overlaps.
# EIGEN_SUBNET=172.30.0.0/24
# EIGEN_UNBOUND_IP=172.30.0.254
# The Compose project name, before the first setup. Unset, it is the install folder's name.
# COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=eigen
# A registry mirror or a private copy of the images: download the eigen command by hand, write this key into
# .env.production, then run ./eigen setup; the installer script refuses a folder that already has the file.
# EIGEN_REGISTRY=ghcr.io/eigen-is/eigen
# The outgoing mail queue: seconds between checks, the queued messages that warn the organization owner, and
# seconds before that warning repeats.
# QUEUE_CHECK_INTERVAL=300
# QUEUE_ALERT_THRESHOLD=200
# QUEUE_ALERT_COOLDOWN=21600
# A public demo, and the admin password its reset seeds (unset, it prints a random one). See docs/DEMO_MODE.md.
# EIGEN_DEMO=1
# EIGEN_DEMO_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
